    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="24">
        <head>Af Rb 24</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="24" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="18" ed="#liebermann"/>XXII. Be nietena<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Rubrics-Af_24.lnote.oe.7"/> misdædum.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="24" corresp="#wit-ot-frag"><pb n="18" ed="#liebermann"/>… Be nietena misdædum.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="24" corresp="#wit-g-prol"><pb n="18" ed="#liebermann"/>XXII. Be nytena<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Rubrics-Af_24.lnote.oe.9"/> misdædum.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="24" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="19" ed="#liebermann"/>XXII. Be nytena misdædum.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="24" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="19" ed="#liebermann"/>De<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Rubrics-Af_24.lnote.oe.6"/> pecorum malefacto.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="192" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>XXII Be nietena misdædum</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="192" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Be nytena misdædu<hi rend="italic">m</hi></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="19" ed="#liebermann"/>Von Missethaten des Viehs.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Rubrics-Af_24.lnote.de.1"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Of misdeeds of livestock.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="193" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Concerning the misdeeds of cattle</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="193" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/></ab>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Rubrics-Af_24.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">19</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Si hominem pecus vulneret <hi rend="italic">Hk.</hi> De homine qui pecus vulnerat <hi rend="italic">Br</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Si hominem pecus vulneret Hk. De homine qui pecus vulnerat Br</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Rubrics-Af_24.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">18</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">neat. <hi rend="italic">So;</hi> nyt. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">neat. So; nyt. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Rubrics-Af_24.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">19</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">y <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">y on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Rubrics-Af_24.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">41</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘der Rinder’ Frühere. Sind diese allerdings zunächst, so doch vielleicht nicht allein gemeint, wie auch fries. <hi rend="italic">nat</hi>, ahd. <hi rend="italic">noz</hi> weitere Bed. hat. Ælfred übersetzt <hi rend="italic">pecudes</hi> und <hi rend="italic">animalia</hi> auch, wo ‘Rinder’ nicht passt, durch <hi rend="italic">nieten</hi> Oros. 158. 226; Gregor 109. 155. 157; <hi rend="italic">vgl. Wb: neat</hi> 2</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘of the cattle’ earlier translators. Though these are indeed meant in the first place, they are perhaps not meant exclusively, just as Fris. <hi rend="italic">nat</hi>, OHG <hi rend="italic">noz</hi> also have a wider meaning. Ælfred renders <hi rend="italic">pecudes</hi> and <hi rend="italic">animalia</hi> by <hi rend="italic">nieten</hi> even where ‘cattle’ does not fit: Oros. 158. 226; Gregor 109. 155. 157; cf. <hi rend="italic">Wb: neat</hi> 2</seg></note>
      </div>
